<title>MEXICO: Pemex says hopes to end natgas imports by Oct.</title>
<headline>Pemex says hopes to end natgas imports by Oct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-run oil monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said on Monday it hopes to eliminate its natural gas imports due to the recent Cactus gas plant blast by October.</p>
<p>Pemex said in a statement it is currently importing 180 million cubic feet of natural gas per day, a figure it hopes to reduce to 60 million cubic feet per day by September before eliminating them entirely the following month.</p>
</text>
